{
 "_about": "Every slice room the SceneRouter can load (slice mode: GameMode.rooms_id = slice/rooms). Same shape as world/rooms.json plus the ActionRoom keys of docs/slice/slice_tech_plan.md 2.2: kind (town / dungeon / arena), camera (diorama / orbit), combat, look_profile, form, robots, checkpoint, autosave, music, spawns, default_spawn. The night market (VS-14, docs/maps/night_market.md): nine town rooms, scenes made by scripts/tools/make_market_rooms.py. look_profile is grim_ps2 until the Technical Artist's market_ps2 profile exists (VS-39); then change the nine strings. start_room is where a New Game begins (Red's hideout, spawn 'start'). pending_rooms: rooms that doors already point at but that are not built yet (the junkyard, VS-17 on); the rooms test accepts them only while they are listed here, with the spawns the door needs. The junkyard (VS-20, docs/maps/junkyard.md): junk_j1 to junk_j4 on foot, scenes by scripts/tools/make_junkyard_rooms.py. look_profile is grim_ps2 until the Technical Artist's junkyard_ps2 and arena_ps2 profiles exist. Encounters are not in 'enemies' here: who fights is data/slice/encounters.json (marker nodes in each scene), waiting for the encounter runner. Kasp's arena (VS-29, docs/maps/kasp_arena.md): kasp_arena, one scene at two scales, made by scripts/tools/make_kasp_arena.py; look_profile is grim_ps2 until arena_ps2 exists. pending_rooms now lists only junk_j5 (the Smash Run, VS-22), which kasp_arena's from_j5 and junk_j4's from_j5 stand in for.",
